.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
See the module.
.PP
\fBResizable\fR: a frame of a given size with a drag handle, like a textarea's grip. The content is laid out at the frame's size, so a responsive component inside (a \fBMetaComponent\fR, a table, an app shell) can be tried at any width and height without resizing the window.
.PP
Controlled: the app owns the \fBSize\fR and takes it from \fBon_resize\fR; the drag rules are \fBprimitives::resize\fR (min / max, a grid, snapping the width to breakpoints).
.PP
.nf
.RS
Resizable::new(meta_component, self.frame)        // frame: iced::Size
    .on_resize(Msg::Frame)
    .constraints(Constraints::new(Size::new(220.0, 120.0), Size::new(900.0, 500.0))
        .snap_to(breakpoints, 8.0))
.RE
.fi
.PP
The frame is clamped to the room its parent gives it, and \fBon_resize\fR then reports the size it actually got (once, on the next redraw), so the app's \fBSize\fR never claims more than is shown. The handle is the bottom\-right corner by default (\fBGrip\fR for the edges and other corners).
